<title>SPAIN: Spain pensions up 2.6 pct as inflation adjustment.</title>
<headline>Spain pensions up 2.6 pct as inflation adjustment.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain said on Friday it had approved an increase of 2.6 percent in pension payments as an inflation readjustment.</p>
<p>&quot;The government approved the revaluation of pensions by 2.6 percent,&quot; said government spokesman Miguel Angel Rodriguez.</p>
<p>&quot;The inflation readjustment will be the first announcement each year by the government,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>In November, the latest data available, the inflation rate was 3.2 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>-- Corresponsalia de Madrid, + 34 1 585-8308</p>
